---
source: crates/bitnet-cli/tests/cli_snapshot_tests.rs
expression: help
---
Run multiple prompts in one resident Apple M4 CPU/NEON SLM session

Usage: bitnet mac chat [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Configuration file path
      --prompt <TEXT>
          Prompt to answer. Repeat for each turn in the resident Mac session
  -d, --device <DEVICE>
          Device/backend label (cpu, cuda/gpu, hip/rocm, oneapi, npu/openvino-npu, nvidia-rtx-5070-ti-cuda/wgpu, metal/mpsgraph, apple-m4-metal, apple-m4-mpsgraph, apple-m4-cpu-neon, auto). Apple M4 labels are distinct proof lanes
      --stdin
          Read additional prompts from stdin, one non-empty line per turn
      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
      --model-id <MODEL_ID>
          Supported model id. Defaults to the validated Apple M4 SLM runtime artifact [default: qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q8_0]
      --cache-dir <PATH>
          Override model cache root. Defaults to ~/.cache/bitnet-rs/models
      --batch-size <SIZE>
          Batch size for processing
      --system <TEXT>
          Optional system prompt
      --max-new-tokens <MAX_NEW_TOKENS>
          Maximum new tokens to generate per prompt [default: 64] [aliases: --max-tokens, --n-predict]
      --temperature <TEMPERATURE>
          Temperature for sampling. The Mac wrapper defaults to deterministic greedy [default: 0]
      --top-k <TOP_K>
          Top-k sampling. The Mac wrapper defaults to greedy top-1 behavior [default: 1]
      --top-p <TOP_P>
          Top-p sampling [default: 1]
      --repetition-penalty <REPETITION_PENALTY>
          Repetition penalty [default: 1.1]
      --seed <SEED>
          Random seed for reproducibility
      --threads <THREADS>
          Number of CPU threads to use (0 = all cores; deterministic mode may override) [default: 0]
      --no-stream
          Do not stream generated token text to stdout
      --progress
          Emit operator progress lines to stderr while keeping token text on stdout
      --quiet
          Suppress warm-session status/progress lines; token streaming still uses stdout
      --allocation-audit
          Include scoped hot-loop allocation counter deltas in session receipts
      --json-out <PATH>
          Output aggregate Mac chat session receipt [default: target/apple-m4-continuity/mac-chat.json]
  -h, --help
          Print help
